 It is an inflammatory or demyelinating disorder of the optic nerve. It is classified into Papillitis, Neuroretinitis, and Retrobulbar neuritis. Clinical features include decreased visual acuity, sluggish pupillary reaction (RAPD), and impaired colour vision.

