- Reactionary haemorrhage following tonsillectomy.

*b) What are the causes of this condition?*


1) Failure to ligate all bleeding points.

2) Slipping of a loosely tied knot or clot following rise of BP.

3) Collapsed vessels opening up.

4) Bleeding from vessels after relaxation of stretched faucial tissue.

